./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:30981:OpenDocument producers need not produce<text:soft-page-break> elements. They may include them if they have computed a paginated layout. Consumers may handle the element while computing the layout, but it shall not depend on its existence. Soft page breaks are only defined for text documents.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:30987:Producers that compute a paginated layout of a document should provide a facility for the export of soft page breaks for the purposes of consistent page breaks and for conversion to talking book formats ( [DAISY]).
